<title>FRANCE: French stock trading hits record high on Friday.</title>
<headline>French stock trading hits record high on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French Bourses' Association SBF said that Friday's share turnover was the highest ever reached.</p>
<p>&quot;Total turnover in French shares was 12.8 billion francs. That is an historic record and exceeds the previous record of 12.289 billion reached in July 30, 1993,&quot; an SBF spokesman said.</p>
<p>Total volume, including foreign shares listed in France, was 13.2 billion francs.</p>
<p>The spokesman said that trading volume was boosted by Roussel-Uclaf, whith Germany's Hoechst making a buy-out bid. Volume is Roussel alone was 4.7 billion francs on Friday, the SBF added.</p>
</text>
